\begin{lemma}[Interior regularity of the minimizing disk]
\label{lem:annular-disk-interior}
\uses{lem:annular-disk-minimum,lem:annular-disk-conformal}
\lean{PoincareMT.M65Interior.localMinimum_energy_power_decay,PoincareMT.M65Boundary.quadratic_holder_contDiffAt,PoincareMT.m65PlateauInteriorRegularityInput_proved}
The same weak minimum has a smooth harmonic representative on
the open disk, with the original weak values and derivatives.
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
Trace-preserving replacement gives local energy minimality.
Coning a small-oscillation boundary trace in a target chart gives
$E(r)\leq CrE'(r)$; if its oscillation is large, Cauchy--Schwarz
gives the same estimate. Integration yields power decay and a
Holder representative. The quadratic harmonic-map equation
improves the weighted energy exponent; after finitely many
steps the logarithmic-potential gradient is continuous.
The equation then bootstraps the same map to smoothness.
\end{proof}

